cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Predicting Tourism Recovery Duration Following Natural Disasters in Sri Lanka"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
authors:
  - family-names: Samarakkody
    given-names: Hashan
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashan-Samarakkody/Neural-Networks-and-Deep-Learning-Research"
abstract: >
  Machine learning pipeline for predicting monthly tourism recovery duration
  after natural disasters in Sri Lanka (2000–2025). Uses seasonally adjusted
  counterfactual baselines, nested cross-validation, and tree-SHAP explainability.
  Covers 60 disaster events from EM-DAT with SLTDA monthly arrivals data.
keywords:
  - tourism recovery
  - natural disasters
  - machine learning
  - Sri Lanka
  - survival analysis
license: MIT
